# Third-party notices

`idna` is a library, never shipped as a compiled binary — imported source, not
run. It vendors third-party code under `internal/x/`, pinned per `VENDOR`. This
file reproduces each vendored component's copyright notice and license text so
that any consumer who *does* ship a binary importing `idna` can propagate the
notice, satisfying BSD-3-Clause clause 2 at the layer that actually
redistributes a binary. The upstream notice also travels in the source tree
itself (`internal/x/net/LICENSE`, `internal/x/text/LICENSE`), per clause 1.

